            <ArticleTitle>Design, synthesis and biological evaluation of six dinuclear platinum(II) complexes.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>963-966</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">S0960-894X(16)31362-2</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.bmcl.2016.12.084</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Six dinuclear platinum(II) complexes with a chiral tetradentate ligand, (1R,1'R,2R,2'R)-N1,N1'-(1,4-phenylenebis(methylene))dicyclohexane-1,2-diamine, have been designed, synthesized and characterized. In vitro cytotoxicity evaluation of these metal complexes against human A549, HCT-116, MCF-7 and HepG-2 cell lines have been carried out. All compounds showed antitumor activity to HepG-2, HCT-116 and A549. Particularly, compounds A1 and A2 exhibited significant better activity than other four compounds and A2 even showed comparable cytotoxicity to cisplatin against HepG-2 cell line.</AbstractText>
